# prompt.history — meaningful prompts and design decisions

## 1. [2026-04-12] Auth expiry detection + --reauth for --update

User ran `--update --verbose` on 262 playlist folders and hit auth expired errors on every single folder — no fail-fast.

Prompts:
- "does this mean notebooklm auth expires?" — yes, Google session cookies expire
- "I want to implement this notebooklm status, to prevent all auth failure in case the auto expires, btw, give me a --reauth that copy the auth data again and overwrite the current one"
- "did you upgrade the code?" — realized script is a symlink, changes are live
- "but I didn't get the new update benefit, still error all the way" — pre-flight said OK but subprocesses still failed

Key discoveries & fixes:
1. `notebooklm status` is offline-only (reads context.json cache), never hits network — useless for auth validation
2. `notebooklm list` hits network but returns exit code 0 on auth failure — error is in JSON body `"error": true`
3. Pre-flight was testing global `~/.notebooklm/` auth, but subprocesses use local `.notebooklm/` copies (stale)
4. `notebooklm auth` was renamed to `notebooklm login` in newer CLI versions

Final design:
- `check_auth_valid()` uses `notebooklm list --json` and checks both exit code and JSON `"error"` field
- `run_update()` pre-flight tests with a real local folder's `.notebooklm/` auth (not global)
- If local is stale but global is valid → auto-runs `run_reauth()` to refresh all copies (no manual `--reauth` needed)
- If both expired → fail fast with "run notebooklm login"
- `--reauth` flag available as standalone for manual refresh

## 2. [2026-04-15] Fix --update summary: only list genuine new uploads

User ran `--update` and got a summary where 4 "updated" folders listed far more "+ [###] title" entries than videos actually added. For MIT microeconomics, the summary showed 49 lines but only 1 new video was actually inserted.

Prompts:
- "what happened to that 4 updates?" — confused by inflated title lists under each updated folder
- "if only 1 video inserted to the playlist, everyone's name is re-indexed/re-numbered, but I don't care the new numbering for existing video, I just want to know the newly added/inserted video and what is the playlist or folder name."

Root cause:
- `run_update()` extracted new-upload titles with regex `→ (\[\d+\] .+)`, which also captured reindex output
- Reindex emits `→ [###] title` three times per run: (1) dry-run plan listing, (2) execution `... OK` lines, (3) text-back-to-video-effort renames
- So a single new insert that triggers renumbering of N existing sources produced ~2N+1 "+ ..." lines in summary

Fix:
- Tightened regex to `^ {8}→ (\[\d+\] .+)$` with re.MULTILINE
- Genuine YouTube upload rename (line ~3276) uses 8-space indent with arrow at start of line
- Reindex lines all use 2-space indent with `old_label → ...` (text before arrow) → now excluded
- Whisper detection unchanged (distinct `Adding transcript as text source:` marker)

## 3. [2026-04-17] Fix SSH port 22 for genesis + --notebook-url takeover of manually-imported notebooks

Two unrelated issues bundled into one session.

### 3a. SSH port 22 fix
User noticed `--remote-sshfs` whisper fallback was failing with `Connection refused` on port 22922 even though genesis listens on 22.

Prompt:
- "still using port 22922?" — pointing at repeated SSH upload failures in the trace

Root cause:
- User had previously edited local `/etc/services` to rename ssh → 22922 for security
- That changes what `ssh`/`scp`/`sshfs` resolve to when no `-p`/`-P`/`-o port=` is given
- Genesis itself still listens on 22, so every default-port outbound call was dead on arrival

Fix:
- Added explicit port flags to all 9 ssh/scp/sshfs invocations in `whisper_via_sshfs()`, `whisper_via_ssh()`, and `mount_sshfs()`:
  - `ssh -p 22 …`
  - `scp -P 22 …`
  - `sshfs … -o port=22,reconnect,ServerAliveInterval=15`

### 3b. Take over manually-imported notebooks with --notebook-url / --setup
User often creates notebooks via YouTube's "Import to NotebookLM" button, then wants the script to take over (rename to `[001]` format, whisper-fill failed videos, etc.). Previously the script could only find-or-create by title, which misses manually-created notebooks with non-standard titles.

Prompts:
- "on --setup (meaning it is not finished), could I manually change which notebook url of a folder pointing to? ... 我只是手動創建 notebook by youtube's 'import into notebooklm', then I want to make you take over the rest manipulation."
- "I prefer a 3rd solution, since I've created that notebook, the easiest way is it's notebook url. could I give you a notebook url, and you know what rest to take over?"
- "how about --setup url (url of a youtube playlist or url of a notebook?)"
- "but if I already in pwd of that implicit folder/notebook, it's index.list has the information (playlist url)"
- "case 3 may be pwd (./index.list) or a path as 2nd argument (notebookurl, path; notebookurl path; path, notebookurl; path notebookurl) this way, not pwd, but path is the folder having path/index.list for us."
- "and with 2 arguments, space or comma must be toleranced."
- "and the bind manually case, usually the folder name, the notebook name are not standardized, we need to perform the rename (Joshua_, no space,etc)"
- "--notebook-url only accept one argument notebook-url? or can take 2nd path of the book folder? and no order (who is in front)"

Design:
- `extract_notebook_id(url_or_uuid)` — parses `https://notebooklm.google.com/notebook/<uuid>[/...]` or a bare UUID
- `classify_setup_arg(arg)` — returns `('notebook', uuid) | ('playlist', url) | ('path', resolved) | ('unknown', arg)`
- `--notebook-url` flag: `nargs='+'`, accepts 1-2 values (URL + optional path, any order, space or comma separated)
- Positional args for `--setup`/`--auto` use the same classification
- Both pools are merged and each token is split on commas, then classified and deduplicated
- `bind_existing_folder(nb_id)` — sets up `.notebooklm/` auth + `notebooklm use <id>` in current cwd
- `standardize_folder_and_notebook(playlist_title)` — renames cwd to `sanitize_folder_name(title)` (os.rename + chdir) and renames bound notebook to `Joshua_<title>` via `notebooklm rename`; no-ops when already standard; skipped if target path exists
- Called automatically whenever `notebook_url` is bound (both classic `auto_setup` with `--notebook-url`, and the bind-existing-folder path)

Supported invocation forms (all equivalent, order-agnostic):
```
--setup <playlist_url> <notebook_url>
--setup <notebook_url> <playlist_url>
--setup "<notebook_url>,<playlist_url>"
--setup <notebook_url> <path>           # uses <path>/index.list
--setup <notebook_url>                  # uses ./index.list
--notebook-url <nb_url>                 # standalone: rebind cwd and exit
--notebook-url <nb_url> <path>
--notebook-url "<nb_url>,<path>"
```

Error cases:
- Bare path alone → "can't know which notebook"
- Notebook URL alone with no `index.list` (and no path) → error asking for playlist URL
- Multiple different notebooks / playlists / paths → error
- Invalid `--notebook-url` value → error
